{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SizeGroupProtocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ObjectProtocol","preciseIdentifier":"s:10GLibObject0B8ProtocolP"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/BuildableProtocol","preciseIdentifier":"s:3Gtk17BuildableProtocolP","text":"BuildableProtocol"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is typically useful when you want a column of widgets to have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same size, but you can’t use a [class"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/Grid"},{"type":"text","text":"] or [class"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/Box"},{"type":"text","text":"]."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In detail, the size requested for each widget in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GtkSizeGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the maximum of the sizes that would have been requested for each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"widget in the size group if they were not in the size group. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"#method@Gtk.SizeGroup.set_mode"},{"type":"text","text":" of the size group determines"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether this applies to the horizontal size, the vertical size, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"both sizes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that size groups only affect the amount of space requested, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the size that the widgets finally receive. If you want the widgets in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GtkSizeGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" to actually be the same size, you need to pack them in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such a way that they get the size they request and not more. In"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"particular it doesn’t make a lot of sense to set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"#method@Gtk.Widget.set_hexpand"},{"type":"text","text":" on the widgets that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are members of a size group."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GtkSizeGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" objects are referenced by each widget in the size group,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so once you have added all widgets to a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GtkSizeGroup"},{"type":"text","text":", you can drop"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the initial reference to the size group with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"[method"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GObject.Object.unref"},{"type":"text","text":"]. If the widgets in the size group are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subsequently destroyed, then they will be removed from the size group"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and drop their references on the size group; when all widgets have been"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"removed, the size group will be freed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Widgets can be part of multiple size groups; GTK will compute the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"horizontal size of a widget from the horizontal requisition of all widgets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that can be reached from the widget by a chain of size groups with mode"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"[enum"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gtk.SizeGroupMode.HORIZONTAL"},{"type":"text","text":"] or [enum"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gtk.SizeGroupMode.BOTH"},{"type":"text","text":"], and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the vertical size from the vertical requisition of all widgets that can be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reached from the widget by a chain of size groups with mode"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"[enum"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gtk.SizeGroupMode.VERTICAL"},{"type":"text","text":"] or [enum"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gtk.SizeGroupMode.BOTH"},{"type":"text","text":"]."}]},{"anchor":"Size-groups-and-trading-height-for-width","level":1,"type":"heading","text":"Size groups and trading height-for-width"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":":"},{"type":"text","text":" warning"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Generally, size groups don’t interact well with widgets that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trade height for width (or width for height), such as wrappable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"labels. Avoid using size groups with such widgets."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A size group with mode [enum"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gtk.SizeGroupMode.HORIZONTAL"},{"type":"text","text":"] or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"[enum"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gtk.SizeGroupMode.VERTICAL"},{"type":"text","text":"] only consults non-contextual sizes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of widgets other than the one being measured, since it has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"knowledge of what size a widget will get allocated in the other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"orientation. This can lead to widgets in a group actually requesting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"different contextual sizes, contrary to the purpose of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GtkSizeGroup"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In contrast, a size group with mode [enum"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gtk.SizeGroupMode.BOTH"},{"type":"text","text":"] can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"properly propagate the available size in the opposite orientation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when measuring widgets in the group, which results in consistent and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accurate measurements."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In case some mechanism other than a size group is already used to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ensure that widgets in a group all get the same size in one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"orientation (for example, some common ancestor is known to allocate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same width to all its children), and the size group is only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"really needed to also make the widgets request the same size in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other orientation, it is beneficial to still set the group’s mode to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"[enum"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gtk.SizeGroupMode.BOTH"},{"type":"text","text":"]. This lets the group assume and count"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on sizes of the widgets in the former orientation being the same,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which enables it to propagate the available size as described above."}]},{"anchor":"Alternatives-to-size-groups","level":1,"type":"heading","text":"Alternatives to size groups"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Size groups have many limitations, such as only influencing size"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requests but not allocations, and poor height-for-width support. When"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"possible, prefer using dedicated mechanisms that can properly ensure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that the widgets get the same size."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Various container widgets and layout managers support a homogeneous"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"layout mode, where they will explicitly give the same size to their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"children (see [property"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/Box"},{"type":"text","text":"]). Using homogeneous mode"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can also have large performance benefits compared to either the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"container in non-homogeneous mode, or to size groups."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"[class"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/Grid"},{"type":"text","text":"] can be used to position widgets into rows and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"columns. Members of each column will have the same width among them;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"likewise, members of each row will have the same height. On top of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that, the heights can be made equal between all rows with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"[property"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/Grid"},{"type":"text","text":"], and the widths can be made equal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between all columns with [property"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/Grid"},{"type":"text","text":"]."}]},{"anchor":"GtkSizeGroup-as-GtkBuildable","level":1,"type":"heading","text":"GtkSizeGroup as GtkBuildable"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Size groups can be specified in a UI definition by placing an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<object>"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"class=\"GtkSizeGroup\""},{"type":"text","text":" somewhere in the UI definition. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"widgets that belong to the size group are specified by a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<widgets>"},{"type":"text","text":" element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that may contain multiple "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<widget>"},{"type":"text","text":" elements, one for each member of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size group. The ”name” attribute gives the id of the widget."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An example of a UI definition fragment with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GtkSizeGroup"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"xml","code":["<object class=\"GtkSizeGroup\">","  <property name=\"mode\">horizontal<\/property>","  <widgets>","    <widget name=\"radio1\"\/>","    <widget name=\"radio2\"\/>","  <\/widgets>","<\/object>"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/SizeGroupProtocol"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol exposes the methods and properties of an underlying "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GtkSizeGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The default implementation of these can be found in the protocol extension below."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For a concrete class that implements these methods and properties, see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/SizeGroup"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Alternatively, use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/SizeGroupRef"},{"type":"text","text":" as a lighweight, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unowned"},{"type":"text","text":" reference if you already have an instance you just want to use."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gtk\/sizegroupprotocol"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/BuildableProtocol","doc:\/\/Gtk\/4GLib14PointerWrapperP","doc:\/\/Gtk\/10GLibObject0B8ProtocolP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/SizeGroup","doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/SizeGroupRef"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforming Types","type":"conformingTypes"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/SizeGroupProtocol","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Groups widgets together so they all request the same size."}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SizeGroupProtocol"}],"title":"SizeGroupProtocol","roleHeading":"Protocol","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"protocol","externalID":"s:3Gtk17SizeGroupProtocolP","modules":[{"name":"Gtk"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SizeGroupProtocol"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk"]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/SizeGroupProtocol\/mode","doc:\/\